\n   \\]\n\n4. **Magnitude Calculation**:\n\n   The magnitude of the ratio is:\n   \\[\n   \\left|\\frac{z_{n+1}}{z_n}\\right| = \\left|\\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{3}i}{4}\\right| = \\frac{\\sqrt{1^2 + 3}}{4} = \\frac{\\sqrt{4}}{4} = \\frac{1}{2}.\n   \\]\n   Hence,\n   \\[\n   \\left|z_{n+1}\\right| = \\left|z_n\\right| \\cdot \\frac{1}{2},\n   \\]\n   and,\n   \\[\n   \\left|z_n\\right| = \\left|z_1\\right| \\cdot \\frac{1}{2^{n-1}} = \\frac{1}{2^{n-1}}.\n   \\]\n\n5. **Combining Terms**:\n\n   Consider,\n   \\[\n   \\left|z_{n} + z_{n+1}\\right| = \\left|z_n\\right| \\cdot \\left|1 + \\frac{z_{n+1}}{z_n}\\right|.\n   \\]\n   Substituting $\\frac{z_{n+1}}{z_n} = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{3}i}{4}$,\n   \\[\n   = \\frac{1}{2^{n-1}} \\cdot \\left|\\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{3}i}{4}\\right| = \\frac{1}{2^{n-1}} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3^2 + 3}}{4} = \\frac{1}{2^{n-1}} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{12}}{4} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2^n}.\n   \\]\n\n6. **Summation Calculation**:\n\n   Let \\( T_m = \\left|z_1 + z_2 + \\cdots + z_m\\right| \\).\n   \n   - For \\(m = 2s\\) (even $m$),\n     \\[\n     T_{2s} \\geq \\left|z_1 + z_2\\right| - \\sum_{k=2}^{s} \\left|z_{2k-1} + z_{2k}\\right| > \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} - \\sum_{k=2}^{\\infty} \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2^{2k-1}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n     \\]\n\n   - For \\(m = 2s+1\\) (odd $m$),\n     \\[\n     \\left|z_{2s+1}\\right| = \\frac{1}{2^{2s}} < \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3 \\cdot 2^{2s-1}} = \\sum_{k=s+1}^{\\infty} \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2^{2k-1}},\n     \\]\n     and,\n     \\[\n     T_{2s+1} \\geq \\left|z_1 + z_2\\right| - \\left(\\sum_{k=2}^s \\left|z_{2k-1} + z_{2k}\\right|\\right) - \\left|z_{2s+1}\\right| > \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} - \\sum_{k=2}^{\\infty} \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2^{2k-1}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n     \\]\n\n7. **Verification**:\n\n   When \\(m = 1\\),\n   \\[\n   T_1 = \\left|z_1\\right| = 1 > \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n   \\]\n\n   Thus \\(C = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\) satisfies the conditions above and we also see that $C$ cannot be greater than $\\frac{\\sqrt{